  "description": "Made for winding rural rides and swift cross-town missions, the Côte finds a smooth balance between touring comfort and efficient function. Its 35mm tires are strong enough to handle gravel roads but also roll well on urban routes. If you want to ride your bike everywhere – the office, a weekend tour, a remote lakeside campsite – but only want one bike, the Côte will happily get you there.\n\nReynolds 520 steel frame feels stable and smooth\n\nShimano® R517 mechanical disc brakes perform in all weather conditions\n\nShimano Tiagra components privide crisp shifting\n\n10-speed drivetrain provide ample gear range for commuting, road riding, and touring\n\nThreaded fittings to attach racks, fenders, and water bottles\n\nLots of clearance between the frame and wheel accommodate fenders\n\nAlex AClass CXD5s tubeless-ready disc brake wheels are designed for the rigors of cyclocross, with heat-treated alloy rims, aluminum hubs and sealed bearings\n\nBig 35C tires work well on unpaved roads and potholed city streets\n\nBikes are covered by MEC's Rocksolid Guarantee and Bike Service Agreement. You can bring your bike to any MEC Bike Shop for free adjustments and minor maintenance for a year after purchase\n\nMEC bikes were designed in Canada. Everything from the frames to the graphics was developed at the MEC Head Office in Vancouver, BC",
